{# Plain-text alternative (SPEC §6.5).

   Not an afterthought. Some mail clients are configured to prefer text, some strip HTML
   entirely, and a message with no text part scores worse with spam filters — which for a recall
   email means it does not arrive, and the patient does not come in.

   WHITESPACE IS CONTENT HERE. The renderer runs Jinja with trim_blocks and lstrip_blocks, so
   every `{% ... %}` tag on its own line consumes the newline that follows it. That is what keeps
   the template readable, but it means blank lines between paragraphs have to be written
   explicitly — otherwise the output arrives as one run-on block with the clinic name, phone
   number and website concatenated into a single unreadable line.

   The wording matches the HTML version exactly. A text part that differs from the HTML part is
   both a red flag to spam filters and a genuine inconsistency for whoever reads it.
#}
Hi {{ first_name }},

This is a friendly reminder from {{ clinic_name }} that it may be time to schedule
your annual visit.

{% if clinic_phone %}
Please contact our office at {{ clinic_phone }}{% if scheduling_url %} or use the link below{% endif %}.
{% elif scheduling_url %}
Please use the link below to book a time that suits you.
{% else %}
Please contact our office to book a time that suits you.
{% endif %}
{% if scheduling_url %}

Schedule an appointment: {{ scheduling_url }}
{% endif %}
{% if reminder_signature %}

{{ reminder_signature }}
{% endif %}

{{ clinic_name }}
{% if clinic_phone %}
{{ clinic_phone }}
{% endif %}
{% if clinic_website %}
{{ clinic_website }}
{% endif %}

--
You are receiving this because you are a patient of {{ clinic_name }}.
To stop receiving these reminders, visit:
{{ unsubscribe_url }}
